# tests/run-and-update-ref, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3):
# evaluating this directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test runs.
#
# A WORKER TEST, in dev/worker-test rather than std/bash: the subject is a
# worker that UPDATES A REF, so observing it means reading refs on the server,
# and that is the one thing caos gives a worker no verb for. Everything else the
# client was doing — curry, prepare-request, run — a worker does directly.
#
# `prepare.sh` is gone with it. It existed to make a worker call
# `prepare-request` on a curried image; this script IS a worker, so it makes
# that call itself.
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/worker-test --worker1:@=worker.sh --bash:@=DEEP-DEPS/bash --updater:@=DEEP-DEPS/run-and-update-ref --succeed:@=succeed.sh --fail:@=fail.sh
